Package: ChronicWolfDeer
Title: Wolf-CWD SIP Meta-Population Model for Wisconsin White-Tailed Deer
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("First", "Last", , "first.last@example.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A multi-compartment, sex-age structured, discrete-time
    meta-population model that tracks white-tailed deer demography and
    chronic wasting disease (CWD) prevalence across Wisconsin counties.
    Each annual step applies density-dependent recruitment and survival
    (Lefkovitch projection), frequency-dependent animal-to-animal
    transmission (SIP: susceptible-infected-perished), and male-yearling
    dispersal between counties. Survival integrates harvest, non-harvest,
    and class-selective wolf predation. The package provides the core
    one-step engine, an iterative simulator, tidy/sf output transformers,
    and parameter-scale helpers for model fitting.
